    <section class="content">
      <p>Roy’s background is rooted in technology, business, capital markets, and building through uncertainty. He leads a Nasdaq-listed technology company and has spent his career hiring people, meeting payroll, raising capital, and making decisions where the consequences are real.</p>
      <p>That experience shaped a simple conviction: confidence is not created by speeches. It is created by predictable rules, disciplined budgets, safe communities, lower red tape, and a government that respects the people who create jobs and pay taxes.</p>
      <p>Roy lives in Vancouver with his family. He is seeking the BC Conservative nomination in Vancouver-Langara because he believes the community deserves representation that is practical, economically grounded, and focused on people rather than bureaucracy.</p>

      <h2>Why public service</h2>
      <p>British Columbia needs leaders who are practical, economically literate, and willing to say that government has limits. A province can be compassionate without being careless. It can invest in the future without ignoring the budget. It can support vulnerable people while still defending public order and public safety.</p>

      <h2>What Roy brings</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Real-world experience.</strong> Years of building and leading companies, not managing press releases.</li>
        <li><strong>Economic literacy.</strong> An understanding of how investment, jobs, and confidence are actually created — and lost.</li>
        <li><strong>Plain language.</strong> A commitment to explaining what government is doing, what it costs, and why it works.</li>
        <li><strong>Community roots.</strong> A Vancouver resident raising a family here, with a stake in getting this right.</li>
      </ul>

